# Next Steps Plan: Shoulder Model Loading Pipeline

## Current Status
- **16 commits** of iterative debugging on the loading pipeline
- Fixed: JSON empty objects, abort() handling, assert→exception conversion,
  face winding, manifold check, vector out-of-bounds in linkMicrotetsToMegatets
- MinimalTest.smd uses simplified params: nTetSizeLevels=1, maxDimMegatetSubdivs=10
- **ShoulderMinimal.smd created** — real shoulder skin geometry with simplified physics
- Extensive debug logging throughout vnBccTetCutter_tbb.cpp and bccTetScene.cpp
- 70 Python tests pass; no uncommitted changes

## ShoulderMinimal.smd Design
- Dynamic object: ShoulderSkin.obj (386 vertices, 768 faces, material 2)
- Deep bed: ShoulderSkin.bed (386 vertices, auto-detected)
- Physics: nTetSizeLevels=1, maxDimMegatetSubdivs=10 (minimal for testing)
- Shader: shoulderFragmentShader.txt (13 material layers verified)
- No static objects or tet subsets (incremental approach)

## Plan

### Phase 1: Verify MinimalTest loads end-to-end ← PENDING USER TEST
- User rebuilds and tests with the linkMicrotetsToMegatets fix (commit 082f6cc)
- Confirm loadScene_debug.log shows full completion through "Lattice: complete"
- Fix any further crashes revealed by the new logging

### Phase 2: Load ShoulderMinimal.smd (simplified shoulder)
- Test with ShoulderSkin.obj + simplified physics (nTetSizeLevels=1)
- This validates the pipeline with real anatomical geometry
- Fix any geometry-specific or scale-dependent issues

### Phase 3: Add static objects and tet subsets
- Add bone OBJs (humerus, glenoid, acromion) as staticObjects
- Add muscle/tendon OBJs as tetrahedralSubsets
- Add tissue regions with per-region physics overrides

### Phase 4: Increase physics resolution
- Bump to nTetSizeLevels=3, maxDimMegatetSubdivs=20
- Then to production: nTetSizeLevels=4, maxDimMegatetSubdivs=40

### Phase 5: Clean up debug logging
- Gate debug log writes behind a #define or runtime flag
- Keep bounds-checking throws and assert→exception conversions

### Phase 6: Load full ShoulderPrototype.smd
- Test with all 7 OBJs, 2752 total faces, production physics settings
- Verify surgical workflow: incision → suture → hook → collision

### Phase 7: Verify original facial models (FacialFlaps.smd)
- Ensure our changes didn't break the primary use case
